1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:07,000
Rule three. Second floor. Beds in the
furniture store. Nobody sleeps on the
ground. I never thought I'd say this,
but I love a mall.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:14,200
Biscuit finds the pet shop on the
first night, and sleeps on the second
floor like a lord. Nobody argues. He
earned it.

3
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:20,400
One of the security screens still
works. Cedar Street. Empty. I watch it
every night anyway. Just in case it
isn't.

4
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:27,233
Day sixteen. The cold comes up from
the floor. Stone, glass, steel.
Everything we touch is colder than us.

5
00:00:27,733 --> 00:00:33,667
We've burned four chairs. The stove
eats a chair an hour. If this goes on
we'll have no furniture and no mall.

6
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:41,067
Then the noise. Every footstep goes
round the atrium and comes back a
second later. Seven people sound like
seventy.

7
00:00:41,567 --> 00:00:48,933
On the island, I could hear the sea
from anywhere. Here I hear the mall
breathing. It's worse, because the
mall breathes in the dark.
